## fm-teardown.test.sh remaining bundle cases
ok - a branch another worktree has checked out never has to be in this copy's bundle
ok - a removed copy's branch is judged by its own bundle, not by the project clone or sibling worktrees
ok - a deleted but still registered worktree does not block a valid recorded bundle
ok - a branch whose registered worktree is gone counts as a side branch the bundle must hold
ok - repeated proofs of one unchanged bundle run the isolated restore once
ok - a changed recorded tip set or changed bundle bytes is proved again, not taken from the remembered restore
ok - the remembered restore is keyed by object format as well as bundle digest and tips
ok - a copy with no local-only commits is not advised to build a bundle
ok - a pushed copy whose only local-only commits sit on a side branch still needs its delivery proof
ok - a HEAD that moves after a bundle admission refuses at final custody without advising a bundle
rc=0
